  "term": "Paxipam",
  "definition": "Paxipam is a synthetic benzodiazepine with anxiety-reducing effects. It works in the central nervous system by enhancing the inhibitory action of GABA at the benzodiazepine–GABA-A receptor complex, which lowers nerve cell excitability.",
